! mcp_bootstrap_p191.strap -- MCP printed page 191: the EOP test for a
! The calling-sequence separator printed on this page is the IBM
! RECORD MARK (vertical stroke, two crossbars, read at 1600 dpi).
! It is written here as "++" -- the convention already set by
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p154.strap, which says in as many words
! that the deck is ASCII.  This deck first printed the glyph
! itself (U+2021) and would have been the FIRST non-ASCII byte
! in a corpus of 180 decks and all of docs/; flagging it rather
! than inventing a stand-in was right, but the stand-in already
! existed.  printed p.152 transcribes the same glyph as ";".
! SEOP control operation (K K EOP), the whole of the I/O reject
! retry loop (K IO REJ), and the first two cards of the backspace
! routine (JBSPE).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.198.  The header was READ, not
! assumed, at 400 dpi:  "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LG000120   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  191".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD READS 221474. <<<
! Six digits, RE-READ AT 1200 dpi, well clear of the dashed rules
! above and below it, printed after the word LOCATION at the
! right-hand end of the heading line.  That is LINE
! 1'S location word (docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1), and
! line 1 here IS a located row -- the case the rule predicts to be
! numbered rather than blank.  Line 1's own LOCATION column reads
! 221474.40, so the two agree on the word and line 1 supplies the
! half.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-EIGHT PRINTED LINES, thirty of which compile.  No SLC, no
! SYN, no VF, NO RESERVATION OF ANY KIND, and no character data.
! The page is CONTIGUOUS from 221474.40 to 221514.40 -- no hole --
! and then blank paper to the foot of the form.
!
!   lines  1-2    two words left over from the density routine on
!                 printed p.190: K DEN OK, the "density set" return
!                 slot, and K CTL CM, the CTL(SEOP) command word
!                 that p.190 line 51 loads with "LX,0,K CTL CM".
!   lines  3-7    the banner and calling sequence for K K EOP.
!   lines  8-19   K K EOP.  It sets a retry count of K REP, calls
!                 K IO REJ through the SIC/B pair on one card,
!                 points $1 at the four-way return vector and
!                 branches to J SEOP T.  The vector is lines 13-16:
!                 EPGK -> K SOS, UK -> RK3, EE -> K SOS, EOP ->
!                 K SEOP R (the slot the caller's SIC fills).
!                 RK3 tests $R.63 and counts down to Z KEOP.
!   lines 20-25   the banner and calling sequence for K IO REJ.
!   lines 26-39   K IO REJ.  A CNOP to get onto a word boundary, a
!                 count of K REP, the SX that plants the caller's
!                 I/O command into the XW on line 29, and then the
!                 EKJ / UNRJ / CBJ tests with their SVA-and-branch
!                 arms.  K K RET on line 37 is the return slot.
!   lines 40-46   the BACKSPACE ROUTINE banner and its linkage.
!   lines 47-48   JBSPE: the count and the LX of the BSP command
!                 word JBSPC, which printed p.192 defines.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ROW COUNT AND SPAN, ESTABLISHED FROM THE PAGE <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! No survey endpoint is quoted here; the brief withdrew them and the
! page settles itself three ways that agree.
!
!   LINE column        1 .. 48, printed, no gap.
!   LOCATION column    221474.40 (line 1) .. 221514.40 (line 48).
!   CARD SERIAL        LG000120 (line 1) .. LG000162 (line 48).
!
! >>> THE SERIAL COLUMN AND THE RECORD MARK ARE THE SAME FACT. <<<
! There are FORTY-THREE distinct serials over FORTY-EIGHT lines.
! Five serials print TWICE, and each pair is two half-word
! statements punched on ONE card, separated by the IBM RECORD MARK
! -- the glyph the listing prints as a vertical stroke with two
! crossbars, "R#B" in line 6 and "RET#B" in line 24 (written here
! as the Unicode double dagger, the only non-ASCII byte in this
! deck; it occurs only inside comment cards and inside "!" notes,
! never in anything the assembler reads):
!
!   lines  9/10  LG000128   SIC,KKRET  #  B,KIOREJ
!   lines 11/12  LG000129   LVI,1,$+1.0  #  B,J SEOP T
!   lines 31/32  LG000148   CB,1,$-1.32  #  B,K REJT
!   lines 35/36  LG000151   SVA,1,K UNR R  #  B,K UNR
!   lines 38/39  LG000153   SVA,1,K CBJ R  #  B,K CBJ
!
! 43 + 5 = 48, and the heading's own "CARD ID LG000120" agrees with
! line 1's serial.  So nothing fell off either end, and the two
! calling-sequence comments on lines 6 and 24 print the separator
! the five double serials imply.  Note that only ONE of the five
! is a SIC/branch pair in shape; the other four are an arithmetic
! or index card and a branch, which is p.184's "one card, one
! WORD" rule again and NOT the SIC-pair rule.  printed p.190
! prints the same mark in its own calling sequence,
! "SIC,K DEN OK++B,K K DENS", so it is a convention of this
! programmer's cards and not a one-page accident.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, BOTH WAYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BACKWARD.  This page prints NO SLC card, so the origin 221474.40
! is ASSERTED.  Three readings support it and none of them is a
! landed deck:
!
!   * the heading-row LOCATION field, 221474;
!   * line 1's own LOCATION column, 221474.40;
!   * the volume OCR of printed p.190 (PDF p.197, a DIFFERENT
!     page), whose last printed line is "221474.00  221476.10 00
!     B,K K EOP" -- a half-word branch at 221474.00, so the counter
!     leaves p.190 at exactly 221474.40.  The same page's line 51
!     prints "221473.00  221475.00 10  LX,0,K CTL CM" and its line
!     52 "221473.40  221502.00 80  SIC,K SEOP R", which are this
!     page's lines 2 and 16 read from the other side.  THE SIC IS
!     THE STRONG ONE: an SIC carries its operand's full 24-bit bit
!     address, so p.190 reads K SEOP R at 221502.00 TO THE BIT, and
!     this deck's counter arrives there independently.
!
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS ASSERTED, NOT CHECKED, AND HERE IS THE EXACT
! >>> CONDITION THAT UPGRADES IT. <<<  Measured: NO landed deck in
! decks/ SYNs any of the nine labels this page defines (KDENOK,
! KCTLCM, KKEOP, ZKEOP, KSEOPR, RK3, KIOREJ, KKRET, JBSPE), so the
! injection test of printed p.177 cannot fire and shifting this
! origin would break nothing.  The moment printed p.192 lands it
! will: its line 1 is "SIC,KKRET" compiling 221512.40 80, and an
! SIC reads its operand to the bit against KKRET, which THIS page
! defines at 221512.40.
!
! FORWARD.  Line 48 is a HALF word (an LX) at 221514.40, so
! >>> THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 221515.00. <<<
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS FOR printed p.192 (PDF p.199) <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   (1) its first LOCATED row is 221515.00.  If it is not, one of
!       us is wrong.
!   (2) its heading-row LOCATION field reads 221515, because its
!       line 1 is a located row and not a banner.
!   (3) its first card serial is LG000163.  WEAKER THAN (1): the
!       brief records two measured serials that print no listing
!       line, both at page breaks, so a missing LG000163 would not
!       falsify the join; a serial BELOW LG000163 would.
!   (4) it DEFINES JBSPC at 221524.00 and J SEOP T at 221525.00,
!       the two symbols this deck SYNs furthest forward, and it
!       REFERENCES three labels this page defines -- KKRET (line 1,
!       SIC, bit-exact), KIOREJ (line 2, B) and JBSPE (line 10,
!       "LB,$13,JBSPE+.32" compiling 221514.72).
!   (5) it prints "BZB,$R+0.63,K SOS" compiling the same word as
!       this page's line 17, "000011.77 80 221274.34 00", with the
!       SAME indicator word and a DIFFERENT written form of the
!       operand.
!
! All five come from the volume OCR of PDF p.199, which is an OCR of
! a DIFFERENT page and therefore a legitimate index, NOT a landed
! verification.  They are predictions, not measurements of p.192.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT WAS RUN, AND WHAT IT REACHED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (The repository moved during this session -- decks/ gained and
! lost a page and tests/check_deck_listing_comments.py was edited --
! so these are the numbers from the LAST run, after the KREP fix.)
!
!   verify_mcp_page.py 191        9 symbols, 30 listing rows, all
!                                 PASS.
!   check_symbol_spellings.py     with this deck copied in beside the
!                                 others: 1544 symbol definitions, no
!                                 symbol spelled two ways.
!   check_deck_listing_comments.py  with this deck copied in: 124/173
!                                 decks carry a parseable block, 4403
!                                 rows parsed, 3096 checks compared,
!                                 0 mismatches.  This deck accounts
!                                 for 30 of those comparisons, so
!                                 EVERY row of the listing block above
!                                 was compared against its own !CHECK.
!   mcp_image.build over pp.99-184 PLUS this page (a scratch script;
!                                 tests/check_mcp_body_image.py was
!                                 NOT edited, see the brief's scope
!                                 rule): merges without disagreement,
!                                 775 defined / 71 external, origin
!                                 0o215000, last word 0o221514,
!                                 ZERO unaccounted words.  Note what
!                                 that last number does NOT say: the
!                                 gap from p.184's 221261 to this
!                                 page's 221474 is jumped by THIS
!                                 deck's origin SLC, and the body
!                                 test's own comment warns that a
!                                 forward SLC makes a missing page
!                                 look accounted for.  The clean
!                                 merge means no COLLISION and no
!                                 DISAGREEMENT, not that pp.185-190
!                                 are present.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS PAGE CANNOT SHOW -- READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A !CHECK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> NO EXTERNAL ON THIS PAGE IS PINNED TO THE BIT. <<<  Every one
! of the nine stand-ins below is read off a BRANCH or an INDEX
! operation, both of which spend their low address bits on their own
! operation field and show only bit 32 (workflow, "WHAT THE ORACLE
! CANNOT SEE", item 1).  There is no SIC and no VFL row on this page
! whose operand is an external: the page's only SIC (line 9) and its
! only two-word VFL-shaped row (line 2, a CTL with literal operands)
! both stay inside the page.  So a passing !CHECK below establishes
! the HALF WORD of an external and nothing finer, and the ".0" or
! ".40" written in each SYN is a convention for the part that was
! actually read.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) "K DEN OK" (line 1), the round glyph between DEN and K.
!     >>> SETTLED ON ANOTHER PAGE'S INK, RENDERED, not on this
!     page's and not on a count of OCR hits. <<<  NOTHING LANDED
!     REFERENCES THIS LABEL, so it is the workflow's exact
!     warning case and was treated as one.  printed p.190 (PDF
!     p.197) PRINTS THE NAME FOUR TIMES and three of them were
!     rendered at 600 dpi and looked at:
!
!       "SIC,K DEN OK"            a located card, mid-page
!       "SIC,K DEN OK++B,K K DENS" the calling-sequence comment
!       "BXE,K DEN OK"            the test that reaches the slot
!
!     In all three the glyph is CLOSED and round, and in the same
!     renders the C of "SIC", "CODE" and "CTL" is open on the
!     right -- so the two are being distinguished in the same
!     impression, which is the only way shape is worth anything on
!     this drum.  The ENGLISH agrees independently: p.190's banner
!     is "DENSITY CHECK", its calling sequence takes a DEN CODE,
!     and the slot is the DENSITY-OK return; this page's line 1
!     comment is "-DENSITY SET".  C22-6728 names the neighbouring
!     routine KKDENS ("Verify that the unit is in the desired
!     density") but does NOT list this label, so the manual cannot
!     settle it.  The volume OCR's 4-to-1 split in favour of OK is
!     recorded but NOT relied on: the brief is right that a count
!     over one drum and one reader is not a vote.
! (2) "SEOP", in the line-2 statement "CTL(SEOP)", in the names
!     K SEOP R and J SEOP T, and in the line-4 banner.  Settled by
!     the TYPESET manuals, which is rung 2 of the ladder: over
!     C22-6678-1 and both revisions of C22-6728 the bare token SEOP
!     appears 134 times and SECP 15, and the compound forms run
!     KSEOPT 22, JSEOPT 5, SSEOP 6 against KSECPT 3, JSECPT 1.  The
!     manual's own section heading is "EOP Test for SEOP I-O",
!     which is this page's line-4 banner.
! (3) The byte of lines 35 and 38, "D0" and not "C0" or "00".
!     Read at 1600 dpi: the glyph has a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT STEM
!     with squared top-left and bottom-left corners against a bowed
!     right side, which is the workflow's C/D discriminator.  Both
!     rows are SVA and both print the same byte, and printed p.184
!     line 21's "SVA,0,K NEW TP" independently prints D0.
! (4) "XW,0" (line 29).  Four characters at 1600 dpi, X W , and a
!     round glyph that is OPEN on the right.  It is a 0: the
!     BINARY OUTPUT column for the row prints "000000.00+ 000
!     000000 000000", an index word whose value, count and refill
!     are all zero, which is what the statement has to say.  Settled
!     on what produced it, not on the shape.
! (5) "JBSPC" (line 48) against "JBSPE" (line 47).  These are TWO
!     SYMBOLS, not one misread: JBSPE is the routine entry (C22-6728
!     lists it -- "JBSPE  Backspace the tape over the label to the
!     load point"), and JBSPC at 221524.00 is the BSP COMMAND WORD
!     whose defining card printed p.192 prints as "JBSPC
!     CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)176.  -BSP COMMAND".  This page's line
!     48 comment is also "-BSP COMMAND", and its LX loads the
!     command into index 0 -- which is exactly the "LX,0,I/O
!     COMMAND" calling sequence line 23 prints for K IO REJ.
! (6) "BZB" (line 17) and the indicator mnemonics BZEKJZ (30),
!     BZUNRJZ (34), BZCBJZ (37).  Each was handed to the assembler
!     as printed and each compiles the printed byte; printed p.190
!     line 33 prints the IDENTICAL card as this page's line 17,
!     "RK2  BZB,$R.63,K SOS" with the same two half words.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED FORMS THAT LOOK WRONG AND ARE NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 28 IS "SX,0,$.32" WITH NO PLUS SIGN, AND LINE 11 IS
! >>> "LVI,1,$+1.0" WITH ONE, ON THE SAME PAGE OFF THE SAME DRUM.
! Measured at 1600 dpi: line 28 is nine characters, S X , 0 , $ . 3
! 2, evenly pitched, with no glyph between the "$" and the ".".
! Line 11 and line 30 ("BZEKJZ,$+1.32") and line 31 ("CB,1,$-1.32")
! all print their sign.  BOTH FORMS WERE HANDED TO strap_asm AS
! PRINTED and both compile the printed word, so this is a card
! spelling and not a defect: "$.32" is the current location with a
! bit offset, 221505.40 + 32 bits = 221506.00, and the row prints
! 221506.01 for index J=0 (2J+1 = 1).  printed p.192 writes the
! other half of the same liberty -- its line 9 prints
! "BZB,$R+0.63,K SOS" where this page's line 17 prints
! "BZB,$R.63,K SOS", and the two compile the identical word.
!
! >>> LINE 2'S "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0($2)" IS THE WHOLE FAMILY'S
! >>> FORM. <<<  printed p.152 line 44 prints "K MODE C
! CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0" compiling "000000.00 8E 000000.15 00".
! This row differs from it in exactly one place -- a second index,
! $2, on the control-code operand -- and the printed byte differs in
! exactly that nibble, 02 against 00.  The .15 is CTLSEOP, which
! p.152's deck checks against RD(SEOP) .11, W(SEOP) .13, LOC(SEOP)
! .17 and plain CTL .05.
!
! >>> NAMES PRINT THEIR BLANKS AND THE BLANKS ARE NOT PART OF THE
! >>> NAME. <<<  The name field prints "K  KEOP" (line 8), "Z  KEOP"
! (line 9), "K SEOP R" (16), "K IO REJ" (27), "K K RET" (37); the
! STATEMENT field spells the same symbols both ways on one page --
! "LCI,5,KREP" on line 8 against "LCI,1,K REP" on line 27,
! "B,KIOREJ" on line 10 against "LVI,1,K IO REJ" on line 33,
! "SIC,KKRET" on line 9 against "BZUNRJZ,K K RET" on line 34.  That
! is C22-6531 printed p.10's alphameric-name rule doing its work and
! it is why the deck writes labels closed up and references as
! printed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK, AND THE DASH COLUMN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Recorded, with NO rule proposed from one page (printed p.147
! proposed one and printed p.151 refuted it the same afternoon):
!
!   * TWO rows carry the asterisk: line 1 (221474.40) and line 32
!     (221510.00).  Line 1 is the page's first row and line 32 is a
!     plain "B,K REJT" in the middle of a run of half words.  The
!     two have nothing in common that the other twenty-eight
!     located rows lack.
!   * Line 47 carries a SPECK in the same column, much smaller than
!     an asterisk and with no arms; line 36 carries one just left of
!     its location.  Called dirt, not ink.
!   * The column between BINARY OUTPUT and NAME prints a SINGLE
!     dash on comment lines 3, 5, 7, 20, 22, 23, 24, 25 and 40, and
!     a DOUBLE dash on lines 41-46.  Lines 4, 21 and 42 (the three
!     asterisk banners) print nothing there.  The split falls exactly
!     at the "BACKSPACE ROUTINE" block, which suggests a change of
!     card deck rather than anything about the statements -- offered
!     as an OBSERVATION, not a rule.  The page that would kill any
!     rule drawn from it is whichever neighbour prints both kinds in
!     one block.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE K REP DATA DESCRIPTION -- AND A CAUGHT MISTAKE <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This deck's FIRST draft wrote "KREP SYN, 30" with no dds, copied
! from decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap, and it merged clean.  It was
! wrong, and the only thing that showed it was re-running the merge
! after the repository moved underneath this session:
!
!   FAIL KREP is declared with more than one data description:
!   (no dds) on printed p.191; (BU,18) on printed p.125.
!
! p.125's line 260 had been changed to "KREP SYN(BU,18), 30" while
! this page was being read, on printed p.185's transcriber's
! finding.  So the brief's rule -- CARRY THE DEFINING PAGE'S dds --
! is not advice here, it is the difference between a page that
! lands and a page that breaks the standing body-image test.
!
! THE dds WAS VERIFIED FIRST-HAND rather than copied from another
! deck's prose: printed p.185 (PDF p.192) line 27 rendered at 600
! dpi prints "000000.00+  +00000036   BU,22 ,10   K REP
! SYN(BU,18),30", and 0o22 = 18, 0o10 = 8.  The same render gives
! three free cross-checks on THIS page's rows: p.185 line 25's
! "SVA,2,K UNR R" prints 221325.45 D0 against this page's line 35
! at 221325.43 D0 (same symbol, J=2 against J=1, THE SAME BYTE --
! a second page settling the D0), line 26's "B,K UNR" prints
! 221314.10 00, the identical half word as line 36, and line 30's
! "B,K CBJ" prints 221275.50 00, the identical half word as line
! 39.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All nine are half-word readings; see "WHAT THIS PAGE CANNOT SHOW".

KREP    SYN(BU,18), 30               ! A COUNT, not an address: lines 8 and 27
                                     ! print 000036 = 30 words.  >>> THE dds IS
                                     ! CARRIED FROM THE DEFINING CARD, which is on
                                     ! printed p.185 (PDF p.192) line 27 and which
                                     ! this transcriber RENDERED at 600 dpi rather
                                     ! than take on trust: "000000.00+  +00000036
                                     ! BU,22 ,10   K REP   SYN(BU,18),30" -- mode BU,
                                     ! length 0o22 = 18, byte size 0o10 = 8.  See
                                     ! "THE K REP DATA DESCRIPTION" above: writing
                                     ! "SYN, 30" here makes the body merge REFUSE.
KSOS    SYN, (8)221274.0             ! lines 13, 15, 17, 19; landed by p.125
KREJT   SYN, (8)221300.0             ! line 32; landed by pp.125 and 157
KUNRR   SYN, (8)221325.40            ! line 35; landed by p.184, which reads it
                                     ! BIT-EXACT off its own SIC
KUNR    SYN, (8)221314.0             ! line 36 B; bit offset unobservable.
                                     ! p.186's defining card (OCR) reads 221314.00
KCBJR   SYN, (8)221313.40            ! line 38; landed by pp.125, 126 and 184
KCBJ    SYN, (8)221275.40            ! line 39 B; bit 32 SET, bit within unobservable
JSEOPT  SYN, (8)221525.0             ! line 12 B; bit offset unobservable.
                                     ! p.192's defining card (OCR) reads 221525.00
JBSPC   SYN, (8)221524.0             ! line 48 LX; an index operation, so bit offset
                                     ! unobservable.  p.192's defining card (OCR)
                                     ! reads 221524.00

        SLC, (8)221474.40            ! NOT PRINTED.  Asserted; see THE JOIN

KDENOK  B,$                          ! line  1 * -DENSITY SET; printed name "K DEN OK"
KCTLCM  CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0($2)   ! line  2   printed name "K CTL CM"
KKEOP   LCI,5,KREP                   ! line  8   printed name "K  KEOP"
ZKEOP   SIC,KKRET                    ! line  9   printed name "Z  KEOP"
        B,KIOREJ                     ! line 10   -ISSUE COMMAND
        LVI,1,$+1.0                  ! line 11
        B,J SEOP T                   ! line 12   -CHECK TERMINATION
        B,K SOS                      ! line 13   -EPGK - GIVE UP
        B,RK3                        ! line 14
        B,K SOS                      ! line 15   -EE - IMPOSSIBLE
KSEOPR  B,$                          ! line 16   -EOP; printed name "K SEOP R"
RK3     BZB,$R.63,K SOS              ! line 17
        CB,5,Z KEOP                  ! line 18
        B,K SOS                      ! line 19
        CNOP                         ! line 26   emits a half word here
KIOREJ  LCI,1,K REP                  ! line 27   printed name "K IO REJ"
        SX,0,$.32                    ! line 28   PRINTED WITHOUT A PLUS -- see above
        XW,0                         ! line 29   -ISSUE COMMAND
        BZEKJZ,$+1.32                ! line 30
        CB,1,$-1.32                  ! line 31
        B,K REJT                     ! line 32 * -IF REPEATED EKJ, GIVE UP
        LVI,1,K IO REJ               ! line 33
        BZUNRJZ,K K RET              ! line 34
        SVA,1,K UNR R                ! line 35
        B,K UNR                      ! line 36
KKRET   BZCBJZ,$                     ! line 37   -RETURN; printed name "K K RET"
        SVA,1,K CBJ R                ! line 38
        B,K CBJ                      ! line 39
JBSPE   LCI,$13,3.0                  ! line 47
        LX,$0,JBSPC                  ! line 48   -BSP COMMAND

