!
! The asterisk counts on lines 4 and 21 were COUNTED, not estimated:
! ink runs segmented at 600 dpi give ten asterisks each side on line
! 4 and twenty each side on line 21, at a glyph pitch of 60.5 px.
! Line 42 prints five and five with no blank before the trailing run.
! The comment cards (lines 3-7, 20-25, 40-46) print nothing in either
! data column and are carried here only as the record; eighteen of
! the forty-eight lines compile nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM KDENOK 221474.40
!SYM KCTLCM 221475.00
!SYM KKEOP  221476.00
!SYM ZKEOP  221476.40
!SYM KSEOPR 221502.00
!SYM RK3    221502.40
!SYM KIOREJ 221505.00
!SYM KKRET  221512.40
!SYM JBSPE  221514.00
!
!CHECK 221474.40 | 221474.50 00 | line 1 K DEN OK B,$ -DENSITY SET -- a RETURN SLOT, not a loop: the caller's SIC overwrites this card's address field, and what the listing prints is the unmodified B,$ at 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50. printed p.190 line 45's "BXE,K DEN OK" prints the same half word for the same symbol
!CHECK 221475.00 | 000000.00 8E 000000.15 02 | line 2 K CTL CM CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0($2) -- the .15 is CTLSEOP in the I/O operation field and 8E's low nibble is index $14; the SECOND byte's low nibble is index $2 on the control-code operand, which is exactly where this row differs from printed p.152 line 44's "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0" (same word, byte 00). printed p.190 line 51's "LX,0,K CTL CM" prints 221475.00 10 and pins this label from the other side
!CHECK 221476.00 | 000036.13 02 | line 8 K KEOP LCI,5,KREP -- 0o36 is the COUNT K REP = 30 decimal, and .13 is 2J+1 = 11 for J=5; decks/mcp_bootstrap_p125.strap line 52 prints the same first word with J=1 and this page's line 27 repeats it, so the two rows are each other's control on the 2J+1 field
!CHECK 221476.40 | 221512.40 80 | line 9 Z KEOP SIC,KKRET -- AN SIC CARRIES ITS OPERAND'S FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so this row READS K K RET at 221512.40 TO THE BIT. K K RET is THIS page's line 37, whose own LOCATION column prints 221512.40, so the two are an internal bit-exact agreement and not a tautology
!CHECK 221477.00 | 221505.10 00 | line 10 B,KIOREJ -ISSUE COMMAND -- target+.10 on K IO REJ, this page's line 27 at 221505.00; the SIC above and this branch are ONE CARD, serial LG000128, split by the record mark
!CHECK 221477.40 | 221500.43 01 | line 11 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- $ is this row's 221477.40, so $+1.0 is 221500.40 and prints 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 3 for J=1. That address is line 13, the head of the four-way return vector J SEOP T selects from
!CHECK 221500.00 | 221525.10 00 | line 12 B,J SEOP T -CHECK TERMINATION -- target+.10; bit offset unobservable. J SEOP T is the SEOP test routine C22-6728 describes ("Continually copy control word until the SEOP bit is off"), and printed p.192's defining card "J SEOP T LCI,14,K REP" prints 221525.00
!CHECK 221500.40 | 221274.10 00 | line 13 B,K SOS -EPGK - GIVE UP -- K SOS at 221274.00, landed by printed p.125; three rows on this page print this identical half word, which is why line 17's second half word is worth having as a fourth
!CHECK 221501.00 | 221502.50 00 | line 14 B,RK3 -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50 on RK3, THIS page's line 17 at 221502.40, so this row pins the label
!CHECK 221501.40 | 221274.10 00 | line 15 B,K SOS -EE - IMPOSSIBLE -- the same half word as line 13 from a different vector slot
!CHECK 221502.00 | 221502.10 00 | line 16 K SEOP R B,$ -EOP -- the EOP arm of the vector and the slot the CALLER's SIC fills; printed p.190 line 52 is "SIC,K SEOP R" compiling 221502.00 80, and an SIC is bit-exact, so the other page reads this label to the bit and agrees with this deck's counter
!CHECK 221502.40 | 000011.77 80 221274.34 00 | line 17 RK3 BZB,$R.63,K SOS -- $R is the right half of the accumulator, word 9 (C22-6531 Appendix A), so $R.63 is 0o11.0o77 and that first half word is a READING of the system symbol, not of a page symbol. The second half word is K SOS at 0o00 OR 0o34. printed p.190 line 33 prints the IDENTICAL card as "RK2 BZB,$R.63,K SOS" with the same two half words, and printed p.192 line 9 prints it a third time written "$R+0.63"
!CHECK 221503.40 | 221476.52 48 | line 18 CB,5,Z KEOP -- 0o40 OR 2J = 0o12 for J=5, so Z KEOP is at 221476.40, which is THIS page's line 9. The byte 48 is the same CB byte line 31 prints with J=1 (.02), so the two rows are each other's control on the 2J field
!CHECK 221504.00 | 221274.10 00 | line 19 B,K SOS -- the third of three identical half words to K SOS on this page
!CHECK 221504.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 26 CNOP -- the counter arrives at an ODD half word here (line 19 ended at 221504.40), so this CNOP EMITS one and K IO REJ starts on the word boundary at 221505.00
!CHECK 221505.00 | 000036.03 02 | line 27 K IO REJ LCI,1,K REP -- the same immediate 0o36 as line 8 with J=1 instead of J=5; byte-for-byte the same word printed p.125 line 52 prints for "KSTAG LCI,1,KREP", which is the strongest confirmation available that K REP is the count 30 and not an address
!CHECK 221505.40 | 221506.01 10 | line 28 SX,0,$.32 -- >>> PRINTED WITHOUT A PLUS SIGN, read at 1600 dpi, and HANDED TO THE ASSEMBLER THAT WAY. <<< $ is 221505.40 and $.32 is 221505.40 + 32 bits = 221506.00, which is line 29's XW; .01 is 2J+1 = 1 for J=0. This row is what plants the caller's I/O command word into line 29 before it is executed
!CHECK 221506.00 | 000000.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 29 XW,0 -ISSUE COMMAND -- an index word whose value, count and refill are ALL ZERO, which is the whole of what "XW,0" can say. It is a placeholder: line 28 stores index 0 over it, and the word then executes as the I/O command line 23's calling sequence asked the caller to load with "LX,0,I/O COMMAND"
!CHECK 221507.00 | 221510.43 44 | line 30 BZEKJZ,$+1.32 -- branch on the EKJ indicator (number 6, C22-6531 Appendix A) and clear it. $ is 221507.00 so $+1.32 is 221510.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o03; line 37's BZCBJZ prints 0o04 for CBJ (number 8) and line 34's BZUNRJZ prints 0o03 for UNRJ (number 7), so the three rows on this page bracket the indicator field together
!CHECK 221507.40 | 221506.02 48 | line 31 CB,1,$-1.32 -- $ is 221507.40 and $-1.32 is 221506.00, the XW again: the loop re-executes the command. .02 is 2J for J=1 against line 18's 0o12 for J=5
!CHECK 221510.00 | 221300.10 00 | line 32 B,K REJT -IF REPEATED EKJ, GIVE UP -- target+.10 on K REJT at 221300.00, landed by printed pp.125 and 157. THIS ROW CARRIES THE PAGE'S SECOND LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK and there is nothing about it that lines 13, 15, 19, 36 and 39 do not also have
!CHECK 221510.40 | 221505.03 01 | line 33 LVI,1,K IO REJ -- .03 is 2J+1 for J=1 with bit 32 CLEAR, so K IO REJ is at 221505.00: the same label line 10's branch reaches and this page's line 27 defines, read a second way
!CHECK 221511.00 | 221512.43 C4 | line 34 BZUNRJZ,K K RET -- UNRJ is indicator 7 and CBJ is 8, and the pair print 0o03/C4 and 0o04/44 against each other on this page, so the ODD/EVEN split of the indicator number is visible in the byte and not only in the address. K K RET is THIS page's line 37 at 221512.40
!CHECK 221511.40 | 221325.43 D0 | line 35 SVA,1,K UNR R -- K UNR R at 221325.40, landed BIT-EXACT by printed p.184's SIC; .43 is 0o40 OR 2J+1 = 3 for J=1. THE BYTE IS D0 AND NOT C0: read at 1600 dpi with a straight vertical left stem and squared corners, and printed p.184 line 21's SVA prints D0 independently
!CHECK 221512.00 | 221314.10 00 | line 36 B,K UNR -- target+.10 on K UNR at 221314.00. This is the symbol printed p.184's deck distinguishes from K UNR R; the two differ by a half word and a bit, and this page prints both within two rows of each other, which is the cheapest check either of them has
!CHECK 221512.40 | 221512.44 44 | line 37 K K RET BZCBJZ,$ -RETURN -- the return slot for K IO REJ: $ is this row's own 221512.40, printing 0o40 OR 0o04 for CBJ. Line 9's SIC reads this label to the bit, so the label and the self-reference check each other
!CHECK 221513.00 | 221313.43 D0 | line 38 SVA,1,K CBJ R -- K CBJ R at 221313.40, landed by printed pp.125, 126 and 184 (p.184 BIT-EXACT off its SIC). Same .43 and same D0 as line 35, which is what settles that byte on two rows rather than one
!CHECK 221513.40 | 221275.50 00 | line 39 B,K CBJ -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50, so K CBJ is at 221275.40, NOT at the 221275.00 a careless ".0" would give; the OCR'd defining card on printed p.185 reads "K CBJ LCI,1,K REP" at 221275.40
!CHECK 221514.00 | 000003.33 02 | line 47 JBSPE LCI,$13,3.0 -- a count of THREE, not a symbol: 000003 is the literal 3.0 and .33 is 2J+1 = 0o33 = 27 for J=13, the largest index this page uses. C22-6728 names this entry: "JBSPE  Backspace the tape over the label to the load point"
!CHECK 221514.40 | 221524.00 10 | line 48 LX,$0,JBSPC -BSP COMMAND -- an INDEX operation, so only bit 32 is readable and the printed .00 says bit 32 is CLEAR and nothing finer. JBSPC is the BSP command word printed p.192 defines at 221524.00 as "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)176." -- the same comment, "-BSP COMMAND", on both cards. >>> THE PAGE'S LAST ROW: it is a half word, so the counter leaves this page at 221515.00
